      "text": "To solve the expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Applying this formula to each pair of terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\n\\]\n\\[\n15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\n\\]\n\\[\n11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\n\\]\n\\[\n7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these results back into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2 = 72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8 - 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we add these values together step by step:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 = 128\n\\]\n\\[\n128 + 40 = 168\n\\]\n\\[\n168 + 24 = 192\n\\]\n\\[\n192 + 8 = 198\n\\]\n\\[\n198 - 1 = 197\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{197}\\).",
